'''''Spiraea betulifolia''''' is a species of flowering plant in the family [[Rosaceae]]. It is primarily native from Eastern Siberia to Korea and Northern and Central Japan.<ref>{{Cite web|url=http://powo.science.kew.org/taxon/urn:lsid:ipni.org:names:30000765-2|title=Spiraea betulifolia Pall. &#124; Plants of the World Online &#124; Kew Science|website=Plants of the World Online}}</ref> The historically recognized varieties native to North America are var. ''corymbosa'', native to a portion of eastern North America, and var. ''lucida'', now known as ''[[Spiraea lucida]]'', native to British Columbia and the northwestern United States eastward to Sasketchewan and the Black Hills.<ref>{{Cite web|url=https://landscapeplants.oregonstate.edu/plants/spiraea-betulifolia|title=Spiraea betulifolia &#124; Landscape Plants &#124; Oregon State University|website=landscapeplants.oregonstate.edu}}</ref>

